{{!-- The Evia mark: an eye that is also an orbit. Pupil, iris, halo —
      seeing, and the whole being seen. Colours come from the CSS.

      Under the Astrolabe variant the same glyph becomes the instrument: the
      halo is replaced by a graduated limb, an alidade lies across it, and the
      pupil reads as the pin the whole plate turns on. The extra parts are in
      the markup always and shown by CSS, so there is no template branch. --}}
<svg class="orb" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <circle class="orb-halo" cx="12" cy="12" r="10.5" stroke-width="1"/>
    <circle class="orb-limb" cx="12" cy="12" r="10.5" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-dasharray="0.7 2.05"/>
    <circle class="orb-ring" cx="12" cy="12" r="6.5" stroke-width="1.25"/>
    <line class="orb-alidade" x1="4.6" y1="19.4" x2="19.4" y2="4.6" stroke-width="1" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    <circle class="orb-pupil" cx="12" cy="12" r="2.4"/>
</svg>
